WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.303
-The president spent the weekend
on an unhinged Twitter rant

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:06.940
after dismissing the rising
threat of white nationalism.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.008
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.476
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.476 --> 00:00:13.379 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:14.914
Well, it's another Monday,

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.584
and that means once again the
president of the United States

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.952
had a quiet, normal weekend
full of hard work

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:22.021
and sober reflection,
and everyone slept well

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:24.190
and woke up refreshed
and optimistic.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.392
And I'm just kidding --
His brain is silly putty,

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:27.459
and we're all doomed.

00:00:27.459 --> 00:00:28.795
-President Trump
spends his weekend

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.096
lashing out on Twitter.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.964
He hit on everything
from the Mueller probe

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.634
to "Saturday Night Live,"
the late Senator John McCain,

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.002
and much more.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.171
He tweeted 50 times
this weekend, alone --

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:41.007
30 original tweets,
20 retweets,

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:44.744
bashing Mueller and the Russia
investigation 14 times,

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.080
also General Motors, Google,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.249
the United Auto Workers,
Hillary Clinton,

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:54.554
and now today calling Joe Biden
another low-IQ individual.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.523
-I mean, Jesus.
His tweets would make more sense

00:00:57.523 --> 00:01:00.960
if they were scribbled on
the wall of a psych ward.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.329
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.632
The bottom of every Trump tweet

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:10.603
should have, "like," "retweet,"
or "send me a free Xanax."

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:13.139
This is insane. The president
of the United States

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.008
tweeted over 50 times
in one weekend.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.876
He retweeted Fox News
a bunch of times,

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.410
attacked John McCain,
General Motors,

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.513
Google, Hillary, and China
all in one tweet,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.214
the Paris Climate Accord,
Obama,

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:24.617
the FBI and CIA, Robert Mueller,
"Saturday Night Live,"

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.051
Hillary again,
John McCain again,

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:28.287
called on Fox News to bring back
a host he likes,

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:30.490
retweeted Fox News,
attacked Fox News,

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.491
the United Auto Workers,
General Motors again,

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:34.193
retweeted multiple
conspiracy theorists,

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.361
a bunch of random people,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.363
accused Democrats
of trying to steal the election,

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.533
and in the middle of all that,

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:44.336
he also found time to tweet
"Happy St. Patrick's Day!"

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:49.608
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:51.677
Which is appropriate

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:55.448
since he tweets like he's
in the middle of a bar crawl.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.983
[ As Trump, slurring ]
Hey, man, I love you

00:01:56.983 --> 00:02:00.686
more than Hillary loves e-mails.

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:03.122
[ Normal voice ] I'm sorry, but
you can't tweet one sane thing

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.625
in the middle of
50 insane things.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.093
It's like if you walked by one
of those guys in Times Square

00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:09.261
yelling "The end is near!"

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.163
and then he turned to you
and calmly said,

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:13.333
"Do you know if there's
a Panera Bread around here?"

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.134
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.134 --> 00:02:16.568
Could use a Panera Bread.

00:02:16.568 --> 00:02:19.505
I'm a little --
a little peckish.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.540
Trump's behavior this weekend
was so unnerving

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.742
that George Conway, the husband

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.511
of white house counselor
Kellyanne Conway

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:27.080
and longtime Republican lawyer
in Washington just tweeted,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.014
"His condition
is getting worse."

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:31.450
And, you know, it really says
a lot about the state

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.587
of our politics that we all know
who he's talking about.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.422
You don't even need to say
Trump's name anymore.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.825
Everyone will know who you're
talking about if you just tweet,

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:42.729
"He's yelling at the TV again."

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:45.197
Trump's Twitter tirade
was unhinged on its own,

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.833
but it's especially unnerving
that he chose to spend his time

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:50.436
attacking everyone
from "Saturday Night Live"

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:53.072
to John McCain just days
after the horrific shootings

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.707
at two mosques in New Zealand.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.008
The gunman was a white
nationalist

00:02:56.008 --> 00:02:57.410
who targeted Muslims

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.545
and was steeped in a culture
of online extremism.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.280
And, yet, when Trump
was asked on Friday

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.315
about the rising threat
of white nationalism

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:05.418
around the world,
he shrugged it off.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:07.286
-Do you see today
white nationalism

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:10.056
as a rising threat
around the world?

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:13.425
-I don't really. I think it's
a, uh, small group of people

00:03:13.425 --> 00:03:15.628
that have very, very
serious problems.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.296
-First of all,
a small group of people

00:03:17.296 --> 00:03:18.697
that have very serious problems

00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:22.034
isn't an answer to the question,
"Is white nationalism a threat?"

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.103
If anything, it's answer
to the question,

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.039
"Who still works
at the White House?"

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:27.273
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.508
Second, of course you
don't see it as a threat.

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:31.744
You called on a ban for Muslims
coming to the U.S.,

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:33.346
and you're trying to
build a wall to keep out

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.847
Mexican asylum seekers.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:37.716
Asking Trump if he sees
white nationalism as a threat

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:41.654
is like asking Joe Camel if
he sees tobacco as a threat.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:44.090
[ Gruff voice ] Well, only if
you're threatened by bold flavor

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.558
and satisfaction.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:46.892
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:48.328
In fact, instead of addressing

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:50.062
the rising threat
of white nationalism,

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:52.231
Trump spent part of his
deranged Twitter bender

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:55.368
over the weekend defending
Fox News host Jeanine Pirro

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.270
and Tucker Carlson
who were under fire

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.272
for making racist
and Islamophobic remarks.

00:04:00.272 --> 00:04:02.175
-Trump tweeting in defense
of his friend,

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.009
"Bring back Judge Jeanine Pirro.

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.445
The radical left Democrats

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.780
working closely with
their beloved partner,

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.182
the fake news media,
is using every trick in the book

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.485
to silence a majority
of our country.

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:15.221
They have all-out campaigns
against Fox News hosts

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.656
who are doing too well."

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:19.959
-"The losers all want what you
have, don't give it to them.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:23.663
Be strong and prosper.
Be weak and die. Stay true."

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:26.432
-"Keep fighting for Tucker and
fight hard for Judge Jeanine.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.134
Your competitors are jealous.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.502
They all want what you've got,
number one."

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:32.371
-The president
of the United States

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.406
is an angry grandpa
who spends his time

00:04:34.406 --> 00:04:37.209
yelling at the TV to bring back
his favorite shows.

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.545
God forbid they ever cancel
"Pawn Stars"

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.913
or he'll have a full-on
meltdown.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.782
[ As Trump ] Bring back Chumlee,
or I'll launch a nuke!

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.183
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.118
[ Normal voice ] Also,
what do you mean,

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:49.155
"Be strong and prosper,
be weak and die"?

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:50.956
You sound like you're about
to ring in

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:53.226
the 74th annual "Hunger Games."

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.227
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:56.596
Also, also...

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.963
[ Applause ]

00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:00.265
Also...

00:05:00.265 --> 00:05:03.402
remember when Trump said
he didn't have time to watch TV

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.104
because he's too busy reading?

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.805
In case you forgot,
he told reporters,

00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:08.274
and this is a real quote,

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.209
"I don't get to watch
much television

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:13.546
primarily because of documents.
I'm reading documents a lot."

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.780
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.016
First of all, you watch
plenty of television.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.885
You got mad at a rerun
of "SNL" this weekend --

00:05:19.885 --> 00:05:21.754
A rerun.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.156
You watch more "SNL"
than Lorne Michaels,

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:26.491
and that's not a joke.

00:05:26.491 --> 00:05:28.961
I have been next to Lorne
when a sketch starts bombing,

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.564
and that man straight-up
leaves the room.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.199
Second,
let's make something clear --

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.334
no one who actually reads
documents ever says,

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.536
"I'm too busy reading
documents."

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:40.105
That's something a lawyer
in a porno says

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:42.774
in the first 30 seconds
of a scene

00:05:42.774 --> 00:05:43.976
where you're supposed to think,

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:47.413
"Oh, maybe
they're not going to do it.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:51.350
I hope I didn't rent a porno
that's just law stuff.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.919
Also, why did I rent a porno?

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:56.154
Oh, right, to support
a local business.

00:05:56.154 --> 00:05:57.356
Don't you quit, Frank.

00:05:57.356 --> 00:05:59.192
I know you're going to
outlast the Internet."

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:00.792
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.792 --> 00:06:02.695
Trump wants us all to think
he spends his free time

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:05.331
in the study smoking a pipe,
poring over stacks of papers.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:06.432
"Mr. President, we need you

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:07.867
to come to your bedroom
and watch TV."

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:10.803
[ As Trump ] Oh, not now, I pray
you leave me to my documents."

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:13.005
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.573
[ Normal voice ] So, the
president of the United States

00:06:14.573 --> 00:06:16.908
decided to spend his weekend
defending Jeanine Pirro

00:06:16.908 --> 00:06:19.111
and Tucker Carlson -- in fact,
Pirro was specifically

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.013
criticized for making
Islamophobic remarks

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:24.584
about Minnesota Congresswoman
Ilhan Omar earlier this month.

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:26.151
The remarks were so heinous,

00:06:26.151 --> 00:06:29.021
even Fox News condemned them
and pulled her off the air.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:31.023
-Omar wears a hijab,

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:35.661
which according to
the Qur'an 33:59,

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:39.465
tells women to cover
so they won't get molested.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:42.568
Is her adherence to
this Islamic doctrine

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:45.971
indicative of her adherence
to Sharia Law,

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:48.207
which in itself is antithetical

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:50.610
to the United States
Constitution?

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.578
-The only thing worse than
saying something that offensive

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:53.912
is saying it that loud.

00:06:53.912 --> 00:06:56.148
Why does she always talk like
she has a bad connection?

00:06:56.148 --> 00:06:58.651
"I said, 'How are things
at college?'"!

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.785
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:01.687
You know, when you say
something bigoted,

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:03.856
you're supposed to whisper it
in private, right?

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:05.691
Jeanine Pirro style would say,

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.860
[ Whispers ]
"You know who I don't like?

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.529
[ Loudly ] Muslims!"

00:07:10.529 --> 00:07:12.765
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:18.171
[ Applause ]

00:07:18.171 --> 00:07:19.771
Then there's Tucker Carlson,

00:07:19.771 --> 00:07:21.841
the bad guy from every
John Hughes movie.

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:24.543
It was reported that he made a
series of racist, misogynist,

00:07:24.543 --> 00:07:27.179
and homophobic comments
on a radio show in the 2000s

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:29.515
hosted by a guy named
Bubba the Love Sponge.

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:32.485
And let me just say,
I was so confused to hear

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:34.987
that Tucker Carlson
went on a show hosted by someone

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:37.623
named Bubba the Love Sponge
that I made the same face

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:39.859
Tucker Carlson makes
every night on his show.

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:41.127
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:43.128
Look at him. He always
looks like he's 30 seconds

00:07:43.128 --> 00:07:45.531
into an allergic reaction.

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.766
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.766 --> 00:07:50.702
"Were there nuts
in this muffin?"

00:07:50.702 --> 00:07:52.638
He looks like he's
three quarters of the way

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.874
to Rudy Giuliani.

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:56.142
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:59.711
Now, anyone who has paid
any attention to politics at all

00:07:59.711 --> 00:08:02.381
knows that Trump has spent years
as a businessman, candidate,

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:05.050
and president openly spouting
anti-Muslim bigotry,

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.486
yet Trump's aides have been
trying to memory hole

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:09.855
his long history of racism
and Islamophobia,

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:12.057
like his acting Chief of Staff
Mick Mulvaney.

00:08:12.057 --> 00:08:14.193
Mulvaney said on Sunday
that he would like us all

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:15.995
to ignore the things
that Trump says

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.163
and focus instead
on what he does.

00:08:18.163 --> 00:08:21.666
-As a candidate, the president
called for a ban on all Muslims

00:08:21.666 --> 00:08:24.604
entering the United States.
He said Islam hates us.

00:08:24.604 --> 00:08:28.907
This kind of language in the
past leads to these questions

00:08:28.907 --> 00:08:31.010
of why isn't the president now

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:33.445
directly using that megaphone
to condemn it?

00:08:33.445 --> 00:08:36.615
-Take the -- take the words
and put them one category

00:08:36.615 --> 00:08:38.350
and take the actions
and put them in another.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.853
-Oh, he's the president,
but we have to separate

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:43.054
the words from the actions
like we're taking out

00:08:43.054 --> 00:08:44.923
the [bleep] recycling?

00:08:44.923 --> 00:08:47.960
Word. Action.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:50.930
Word.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:56.835
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:56.835 --> 00:09:02.140
Word, but it's still got a lot
of spaghetti in it, so action."

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:05.444
And I'm sorry, but his
only actions are words.

00:09:05.444 --> 00:09:07.078
Other than Twitter,
what else does he do?

00:09:07.078 --> 00:09:09.448
You won't let us watch him golf,
even though if you did,

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.082
it would be higher rated
than the Super Bowl.

00:09:11.082 --> 00:09:13.085
I mean, I would watch.

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:14.620
Because there's so much
that I want to know.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:15.954
Is he actually good,

00:09:15.954 --> 00:09:17.956
or is he terrible, and everyone
pretends that he's good?

00:09:17.956 --> 00:09:19.058
I know he cheats, but how?

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:20.992
Is he good at it,
or is he super obvious?

00:09:20.992 --> 00:09:23.296
Does he make a weird noise
when he swings, and if so,

00:09:23.296 --> 00:09:25.998
is it the same noise, or does
it change based on the club?

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:28.000
Seriously, televise
his next golf game,

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.969
sell it on pay-per-view, and
build your wall with that money.

00:09:30.969 --> 00:09:32.871
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:09:32.871 --> 00:09:35.107
And I'm sorry.

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:37.776
I'm sorry, but you don't get
to put Trump's words

00:09:37.776 --> 00:09:39.711
in a different category
unless that category

00:09:39.711 --> 00:09:41.814
is signs you might be having
a stroke.

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:43.448
-Every single car out there,

00:09:43.448 --> 00:09:45.284
even the really
"expenses" ones...

00:09:45.284 --> 00:09:47.586
Controlled by large "derners"...

00:09:47.586 --> 00:09:52.258
10,000 known or "suspested"
gang members.

00:09:52.258 --> 00:09:54.326
-Mulvaney then went on to
claim that despite Trump's

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:56.595
long established history
of anti-Muslim bigotry,

00:09:56.595 --> 00:09:58.697
Trump, himself,
was not Islamophobic.

00:09:58.697 --> 00:09:59.998
-I hear what folks say,

00:09:59.998 --> 00:10:01.867
"Oh, Donald Trump said this
during the campaign."

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:03.869
Look at what we've done
while we've been here.

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:05.237
And I don't think anybody
could say

00:10:05.237 --> 00:10:07.239
that the president's
anti-Muslim.

00:10:07.239 --> 00:10:09.708
-Well, let me try --
The president is anti-Muslim.

00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:12.144
Yep, that was not hard at all.

00:10:12.144 --> 00:10:14.379
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:14.379 --> 00:10:17.349
It was easy to say.

00:10:17.349 --> 00:10:20.019
Certainly wasn't as hard
as saying "suspested."

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:21.253
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:22.587
You know, you're not very bright

00:10:22.587 --> 00:10:24.890
for someone who looks like
grown-up Sherman.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.792
